        "p1": {
          "type": "part",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What we are working towards",
            "body": "<p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA. That standard covers how the site reads to screen readers, how it behaves for keyboard-only visitors, and whether text stays legible when it is enlarged or the colours are inverted.</p><p>Accessibility is not a one-off project. Every time we add a page or change a template, it goes through the same checks.</p>"
          }
        },
        "p2": {
          "type": "part",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What we check",
            "body": "<ul><li>Every image that carries meaning has descriptive alternative text.</li><li>The whole store can be operated with a keyboard alone, and the focus outline is always visible.</li><li>Text and background colours are tested for contrast against the AA thresholds.</li><li>Headings follow a real hierarchy, so screen-reader users can skim the page structure.</li><li>Form fields have labels that are read out, and errors are announced rather than shown only in colour.</li><li>Motion is reduced automatically for visitors whose system asks for it.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "p3": {
          "type": "part",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where we fall short",
            "body": "<p>Parts of the store rely on third-party services — payment, reviews, chat — whose interfaces we do not control. We test them and raise problems with the vendors, but we cannot guarantee their conformance.</p><p>If any part of this site blocks you, that is a defect on our side, and we want to hear about it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "p4": {
          "type": "part",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Tell us about a barrier",
            "body": "<p>Describe the page and what went wrong — the browser and any assistive technology you use helps us reproduce it faster. We aim to acknowledge every report within one business day and will tell you honestly how long a fix will take.</p><p>If you need information from this site in another format while we work on it, ask and we will send it to you directly.</p>"
          }
        }
